Warnings / notes / assumptions:
•	NuGet warnings about some package advisories were emitted (no secrets added). These are informational from the feed; no secrets or credentials were added to source.
•	For PasswordHasher<T> I added Microsoft.AspNetCore.Identity package (an available stable version) to enable hashing during seeding. PasswordHasher produces salted hashes; the seed logic hashes transient demo PINs at runtime and stores only the hash. The hash output may vary across runs because of random salt; the seeding operation remains idempotent with respect to logical records (it does not duplicate records) but hash bytes will differ if run repeatedly — the case study requested using PasswordHasher specifically; if deterministic identical hash bytes are strictly required, we should use a deterministic hashing approach (not recommended for PINs).
•	Migrations were scaffolded as hand-authored artifacts in the repository to represent the intended initial schema (they were not executed against any remote/production database).
•	Connection strings are not hardcoded. appsettings.json contains an empty ConnectionStrings:NovaBanking placeholder; real secrets must come from environment/user secrets per spec.
•	Seeder uses Database.EnsureCreated() to create schema for development/demo only; it does not call EnsureDeleted() or run destructive operations.
